# The release pipeline assembles the server via `git archive HEAD:server`, which
# archives THIS subtree and therefore only reads .gitattributes files inside it —
# the repository-root .gitattributes does NOT apply. Without these rules, a
# Windows dev machine with core.autocrlf=true bakes CRLF into shell scripts, and
# a container entrypoint like `#!/bin/sh\r` fails with
# "exec ...: no such file or directory". Keep POSIX scripts LF here.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
